  "summary": "Britain's Factory Act of 1833 applied to textile factories, with silk and lace producers among those exempt. It barred employing children under nine, required schooling of two hours a day for the young workers, and created government factory inspectors with the right to enter any factory. It did not introduce the ten-hour day workers sought.",
